 ### DE-NeRF
-DE-NeRF decomposes lighting, geometry, and appearance to allow relighting of high-frequency environments and appearance editing [S3]. It trains a signed distance field (SDF) function using a set of 2D images to reconstruct a display grid as the input scene for the MLP. It decomposes the scene into geometric features and appearance features (diffuse reflection, roughness, specular tint). It inputs geometric features, appearance features, and distance $h$ (from sampling point to grid) into four corresponding MLPs to predict diffuse albedo, roughness value, and specular tint. It integrates diffuse reflectance with the environment map to get diffuse color $c_d$. It trains a specular lighting MLP $F_s$ to get specular lighting $c_l$. It multiplies specular lighting $c_l$ with specular hue to get specular color $c_s$. It calculates final color $c$ as $c_s + c_d$ [S3]. On NeRF Synthetic and Shiny Blender data sets, PSNR is 2 points higher than latest papers [S3].
+DE-NeRF decomposes lighting, geometry, and appearance to allow relighting of high-frequency environments and appearance editing [S3]. It trains a signed distance field (SDF) function using a set of 2D images to reconstruct a display grid as the input scene for the MLP. It decomposes the scene into geometric features and appearance features (diffuse reflection, roughness, specular tint). Input geometric features, appearance features, and distance $h$ (from sampling point to grid) are input into four corresponding MLPs to predict diffuse albedo, roughness value, and specular tint. Diffuse reflectance is integrated with the environment map to get diffuse color $c_d$. A specular lighting MLP $F_s$ is trained to get specular lighting $c_l$. The specular lighting $c_l$ is multiplied with specular hue to get specular color $c_s$. The final color $c$ is calculated as $c_s + c_d$ [S3]. On NeRF Synthetic and Shiny Blender data sets, PSNR is 2 points higher than latest papers [S3].
 
 ### RefSR-NeRF
-RefSR-NeRF is a reference-guided super-resolution neural radiation field framework combining NeRF and RefSR-CNN to achieve high-quality new perspective synthesis while balancing memory and speed [S3]. In Stage 1, it modifies NeRF sampling strategy to adopt patch ray sampling on the high-resolution input image to obtain a low-resolution image. RefSR-CNN yields feature maps from the detail-dominant information module and the degradation-dominant information module. It fuses the two feature maps to reconstruct a high-resolution image [S3]. On the NeRF-LLFF data set, PSNR is nearly one point higher than the best paper [S3].
