 ### DiffusioNeRF
-DiffusioNeRF is a method that utilizes a denoising diffusion model to learn priors for scene geometry and color, normalizing the geometry and color of the scene to achieve better quality in reconstructed geometry under sparse input views [S3]. During NeRF training, it renders random RGBD patches. It backpropagates the estimated gradients of the log-likelihood to the color and density fields to normalize the geometry and color [S3]. On the LLFF dataset, the PSNR indicators in 3, 6, and 9 input views are 1-2 points higher. Among three input views, the PSNR index is nearly 1 point higher than ViP-NeRF [S3].
