 ### NeRFLight
-NeRFLight extends grid-based methods by dividing the scene into eight different regions to split NeRF into separate density and color fields, using a shared feature grid [S3]. It avoids increasing the number of features for seamless reconstruction while reducing stored feature values [S3]. It divides the scene into eight different regions, each corresponding to an MLP that outputs density and color. It uses a shared feature grid with features symmetrically placed at the center of the scene [S3].
