 ### Edit-NeRF
-Edit-NeRF is the first method to execute user-controlled deformation models on NeRF, proposing a modular network's conditional radiance field to guide model editing [S2]. It trains on multiple instances of the same category, learns underlying part features in an unsupervised manner, and allows user guidance in 2D image shape/texture to propagate to 3D space [S2]. Its limitation is a limited capability in shape operations; it only supports adding or deleting local parts of an object. The editing process is slow due to its iterative optimization nature [S2].
