 ### DT-NeRF
 In DT-NeRF, both the Diffusion and Transformer models are trained jointly within a unified optimization framework, sharing the same loss function, and are not pretrained but optimized simultaneously during training through backpropagation [S4].
 
+### Deformable Radiance Fields
+Deformable Radiance Fields represent a dynamic surgical scene as a static canonical radiance field and a time-dependent displacement field to handle non-rigid deformations [S5]. Preprocessing maps input coordinates and time into Fourier features using positional encoding $\gamma(\cdot)$ before feeding to the networks [S5]. Color and occupancy at time $t$ for point $x$ are retrieved as $F_\Theta(x + G_\Phi(x, t), d)$ [S5]. The Canonical field $F_\Theta(x, d)$ is an 8-layer MLP with parameters $\Theta$. Inputs: coordinates $x \in \mathbb{R}^3$, unit view direction $d \in \mathbb{R}^3$. Outputs: RGB color $c(x, d) \in \mathbb{R}^3$, space occupancy $\sigma(x) \in \mathbb{R}$. The Displacement field $G_\Phi(x, t)$ is an 8-layer MLP with parameters $\Phi$. Inputs: space-time coordinates $(x, t)$. Output: displacement vector between point $x$ at time $t$ and corresponding point in canonical field [S5].
